WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.693
When the town hall meeting ended, people returned to their homes.

2
00:00:05.694 --> 00:00:10.672
Paul Revere and John Adams stayed behind speaking together.

3
00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:13.761
The children stayed close by.

4
00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:18.517
"Paul, you know what to do," said John Adams.

5
00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.819
Revere nodded and put on his hat.

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.857
"It was nice meeting you,"

7
00:00:23.858 --> 00:00:27.535
he said to the children and then left.

8
00:00:27.536 --> 00:00:30.869
"Where is he going?" asked Vinnie.

9
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:37.405
"Mr. Revere takes important messages to New York and Philadelphia," explained Will.

10
00:00:37.406 --> 00:00:40.404
"That’s what I want to do someday."

11
00:00:40.405 --> 00:00:44.395
"To be a messenger?" asked Vinnie.

12
00:00:44.396 --> 00:00:49.678
"To be one of the Sons of Liberty," said Will seriously.

13
00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:53.756
"Good-bye, children," said John Adams.

14
00:00:53.757 --> 00:00:57.648
"Never forget the value of freedom."

15
00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:01.983
They all shook hands, and the children left.

16
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:07.322
As they walked down Boston’s streets, the daylight was fading.

17
00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:08.733
"Come for supper.

18
00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:12.266
Mother is making meat stew," said Will.

19
00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:17.043
"You have been so kind to us," said Mandy.

20
00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:19.623
"But we should go now."

21
00:01:19.624 --> 00:01:23.690
"Where are we going?" Vinnie whispered to her.

22
00:01:23.691 --> 00:01:28.335
"Thank you for everything," said Mandy to Will.

23
00:01:28.336 --> 00:01:32.340
"Well, you know where I live," he said.

24
00:01:32.341 --> 00:01:34.030
"Visit some time.

25
00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:36.800
You can try our apple cider."

26
00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:42.625
Waving good-bye, the children watched Will disappear down the street.

27
00:01:42.626 --> 00:01:46.811
"That’s just great!" Vinnie sighed.

28
00:01:46.812 --> 00:01:52.763
"Without Will, how are we supposed to find this tree?"

29
00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:56.304
He took the photo out of his pocket.

30
00:01:56.305 --> 00:01:59.660
Mandy was looking up the street.

31
00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:04.056
Two familiar figures were walking ahead of them.

32
00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:08.536
"Vinnie, let me see the photo," said Mandy.

33
00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:10.815
He showed it to her.

34
00:02:10.816 --> 00:02:14.570
The flag in the photo was glowing blue.

35
00:02:14.571 --> 00:02:17.479
"There’s a big tree over there.

36
00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.261
It looks like this one," said Mandy.

37
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:26.310
Mandy followed the two figures, walking just behind them.

38
00:02:26.311 --> 00:02:28.850
Vinnie followed her.

39
00:02:28.851 --> 00:02:35.025
When they got to the corner, the children noticed a sign on the nearby elm tree.

40
00:02:35.026 --> 00:02:38.520
"Can you read it?" asked Mandy.

41
00:02:38.521 --> 00:02:40.330
Vinnie shook his head.

42
00:02:40.331 --> 00:02:43.018
"It’s too far."

43
00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:46.733
The two figures walked into a grocery store.

44
00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:51.402
Vinnie ran up to the tree and quickly read the sign.

45
00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:54.368
Then he ran back to Mandy.

46
00:02:54.369 --> 00:02:59.833
"It says, ‘The Tree of Liberty’," he gasped.

47
00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:02.524
The two men reappeared.

48
00:03:02.525 --> 00:03:06.628
One of the men was Mr. Keith, the grocer.

49
00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:09.185
He held a long pole.

50
00:03:09.186 --> 00:03:13.872
The other man carried a red and white, bundled cloth.

51
00:03:13.873 --> 00:03:18.659
At the tree, they tied the cloth at the top of the pole;

52
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.875
it was a flag!

53
00:03:20.876 --> 00:03:27.213
They lifted the flag high enough in the tree so it stuck out from the branches.

54
00:03:27.214 --> 00:03:31.689
The grocer said, "The Sons of Liberty will meet tonight."

55
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:35.849
"Action will be taken," said the other man.

56
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.312
Then he turned around.

57
00:03:38.313 --> 00:03:40.782
It was John Hancock.

58
00:03:40.783 --> 00:03:46.104
"He’s been released!" Mandy nearly shouted.

59
00:03:46.105 --> 00:03:51.035
"Mandy! The photo!" Vinnie pointed to the picture.

60
00:03:51.036 --> 00:03:56.475
Sticking out of the tree, the red and white flag was glowing brightly.

61
00:03:56.476 --> 00:03:59.422
It was time to go home.

62
00:03:59.423 --> 00:04:08.399
The children’s eyes closed as they fell into the familiar dark tunnel.

